Z||000000||Alex4mula||10-27-2000||05:02 PM||||One of my Formula's CV joint started to make a ticking noise like when two marble balls collide. It does it (or at least I hear it)only launching it forward in 1st or backward in reverse. No noise while running. I'm sure I will need to repair them but how long could it last like that? If there is the risk of it falling appart at any moment? Should I stop using the car?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I guess my 3.4 is finding the weak links already  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||10-27-2000||10:32 PM||||No one had experiences with this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">??||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-27-2000||10:48 PM||||It could be the joint or the big nut on the end of the shaft.<P>The cheap test is replace the nut, it's about $2, and torque it to spec. If the problem stops it was the nut loose. ((It's s lock nut. your supposed to trash it durring service.))<P>Torque the nut with the wheel on and the car sitting on the ground normal. pull the hand brake. You want to eliminate as much movement of the car and suspension as posible or you'll get a bogus torque number. ((You'll need the center cap off on an aluminum wheel))<P>If it's the shaft or joint it could last years or quit tomorow. No way to tell really.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||10-28-2000||03:27 PM||||Thanks theogre. I don't think is the nut because with the wheel off and the car lifted I could hear the clik inside the CV joint housing. Anyway I will check it just in case.||||reg||1
